Phase H.2: register requires_top_cover config key

Snapmaker fork branch `feature_top_cover` (PR #284) introduces a
per-filament `coBools` flag for materials that need the U1's
magnetic top cover installed (ABS, ASA, PA, PC). The fork hooks
this into `Print::validate()` to surface a warning when the
filament has it set + the printer's bed-type hint is "open frame".

OrcaXR Phase H.2 ships only the PrintConfig key registration here
in C++. The user-visible warning is rendered by the Compose shell
in `MainActivity.kt` (see `topCoverHint` derived state) — same
pattern as Phase E's `FilamentRules` (gotcha #28): when the rule
data is small and the trigger is a per-printer / per-filament
combination the UI already tracks, the Kotlin side is the
shorter path. The libslic3r Print::validate() hook would only
matter if a future code path slices without the UI (CLI tool,
scripted automation), at which point we'd add the validate-side
hook then.

Pure additive registration — default false. Profiles that omit
the key behave exactly as before. Anchors after Phase H.1's
`filament_is_high_temperature` block so the two patches chain
cleanly.

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp b/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
@@ -2770,6 +2770,17 @@
     def->mode = comAdvanced;
     def->set_default_value(new ConfigOptionBools { false });
 
+    // OrcaXR Phase H.2 (Snapmaker fork PR #284 port). Per-filament
+    // coBools for materials that need the U1's magnetic top cover.
+    // Default false — open-frame-friendly profiles unaffected. The
+    // user-visible warning is rendered Compose-side; see gotcha #28
+    // for why the libslic3r Print::validate() hook is deferred.
+    def = this->add("requires_top_cover", coBools);
+    def->label = L("Requires magnetic top cover");
+    def->tooltip = L("When set, OrcaXR warns if the printer's bed type suggests an open frame. Helps avoid warping on ABS/ASA/PA/PC prints.");
+    def->mode = comAdvanced;
+    def->set_default_value(new ConfigOptionBools { false });
+
     def = this->add("filament_type", coStrings);
     def->label = L("Type");
     def->tooltip = L("The material type of filament.");
